      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn subagents. Do not invoke live agent tests, push, publish, comment/review on GitHub or merge remote state; explicit GitWeave System Actions handle publication. Never redeem usage-limit reset tickets, buy allowance, or switch models/providers to bypass limits. Stop and return blocked if an actual permission/capability limitation prevents completion; do not invent an unsupported workaround or weaken requirements. Ordinary code/test defects are fixable findings, not capability blockers. Keep project material in English. Use deterministic tests and preserve existing behavior outside the issue's explicit change. Do not alter other worktrees or the original checkout.\n\nImplement the supplied issue and accepted clarification only. Keep the change minimal, preserve unrelated existing behavior, and update focused deterministic tests and current documentation. Do not implement other open Issues in this PR. This issue intentionally simplifies existing behavior; do not recreate the removed policy as a new abstraction.\nImplement the whole supplied issue. Run all relevant deterministic checks. Leave final files for GitWeave to checkpoint. Return ready only after completion, or blocked with concrete details.",
